        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by the `usb clock` being left uninitialized due to the `CLK_SET_RATE_GATE` flag set on the clock drivers, which prevents the clock rate from being changed once prepared. Additionally, the EHCI driver was preparing and enabling the `uhpck` clock, which in turn prepared its parent clock (the `usb clock`), thus blocking any rate changes and leading to the failure of the OHCI driver to set the `usb clock` rate to 48MHz.

        Commit message:
